.\" Manual page of fepx (step 9.8, ROADMAP D101). Installed in share/man/man1 by CMake;
.\" every option of "fepx --help" must be described here (test man_page_options).
.TH FEPX 1 "2026-10-28" "FEPX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fepx \- finite element simulation of polycrystal plasticity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpirun
.B \-np
.I ranks
.B fepx
.br
.B fepx \-\-help
.br
.B fepx \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fepx
simulates the elastic\-viscoplastic deformation of polycrystalline aggregates with a
crystal\-plasticity finite element method, in parallel with MPI.
It is run, without arguments, in a directory that holds the input files; the results are
written to the directory
.I simulation.sim
in the same directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the banner and a usage summary, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version (with the git hash and the date of the commit built, when known), then exit.
.PP
Any other argument is an error. Both options are handled before MPI is started, so they may be
given without
.BR mpirun .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I simulation.cfg
The configuration: the material, the loading, the boundary conditions, the solver and the
output (required).
.TP
.I simulation.msh
The mesh, in Neper's msh format, with the crystal orientations of its element sets (required).
.TP
.IR simulation.ori ", " simulation.phase ", " simulation.opt
Orientations, phases and per\-element\-set or per\-element material parameters, read when the
configuration asks for them.
.TP
.I simulation.sim/
The output directory: the inputs, the result files and, if requested, the restart files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non\-zero when the run stops on an error, whose message is written to the
standard error (and to the standard output of rank 0).
.SH EXAMPLES
The tutorial cases are installed in
.I share/doc/fepx/examples
of the installation
.RI ( $CONDA_PREFIX/share/doc/fepx/examples
for the conda package).
To run one, copy its directory and run
.B fepx
in the copy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cp \-r $CONDA_PREFIX/share/doc/fepx/examples/simple_simulation .
cd simple_simulation
mpirun \-np 4 fepx
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpirun (1),
.BR neper (1).
The manual: <https://fepx.info>.
